{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":48756,"name":"Mark Dickinson","username":"mdickinson","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/mdickinson/{size}/976_2.png","created_at":"2022-03-06T13:16:21.396Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAs the \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-682-format-specifier-for-signed-zero/13596/17\"\u003edesignated PEP-Delegate\u003c/a\u003e for John Belmonte’s \u003ca href=\"https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0682/\"\u003ePEP 682\u003c/a\u003e, I’m hereby accepting PEP 682 for inclusion into Python, targeting Python 3.11. I’d like to thank John for a well-written PEP, and for his patience with the PEP process. I’d also like to thank the PEP editors for their invaluable help with the process. I look forward to a slightly more human-friendly formatting experience in Python 3.11!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn process: I’ll make a PR to update the PEP itself shortly, and then we need to review and merge the reference PR, ideally before the 3.11.0a7 release.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCongratulations, John!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith thanks to all involved,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMark\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2022-03-06T13:24:30.786Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":361,"reads":71,"readers_count":70,"score":1954.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":14088,"topic_slug":"accepting-pep-682-format-specifier-for-signed-zero","display_username":"Mark Dickinson","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0682/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 682 -- Format Specifier for Signed Zero | Python.org","clicks":67},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-682-format-sp